<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <parent>
        <groupId>org.finos.legend.pure</groupId>
        <artifactId>legend-pure-next-platform-java-extensions</artifactId>
        <version>0.0.1-SNAPSHOT</version>
    </parent>

    <artifactId>legend-pure-next-platform-java-extensions-diagram</artifactId>
    <packaging>jar</packaging>
    <name>Legend Pure - Next - Java Platform - Diagram Extension</name>

    <!--
      The `###Diagram` language on this platform: the ANTLR parser generated from the extension's own
      grammar, and its manifest staged where the engine's reader can find it.

      The extension itself is host-neutral — pure/extensions/diagram is grammar plus Pure, exactly the
      pair the Pure language is built from — so adapting it to a platform means generating that
      platform's parser from the .g4 and letting it register. Nothing here is diagram-specific beyond
      the two paths below, which is the point: a second extension is a copy of this pom with one word
      changed.

      WHY THE PARSER MUST BE GENERATED HERE, since it is the thing that was missing: the Pure tests call
      `parseAntlr($source, 'DiagramParser', ...)`, and a host without the generated parser fails with
      "Unknown grammar: DiagramParser". No JVM host had one — Truffle has only M3 and Top as well — so
      those tests failed everywhere but JavaScript.
    -->

    <properties>
        <repo.dir>${project.basedir}/../../../../..</repo.dir>
        <extension.dir>${repo.dir}/pure/extensions/diagram</extension.dir>
        <!-- Where ANTLR generates, and therefore where the engine's reflective lookup finds the classes
             this extension's manifest names. The plugin derives the package from the path below its
             source directory, so the staging below decides it. -->
        <antlr.package.dir>org/finos/legend/pure/platform/java/extensions/diagram</antlr.package.dir>
    </properties>

    <dependencies>
        <!-- The engine: GrammarExtension, Language and the reader. One way only — it never depends on
             this module. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.finos.legend.pure</groupId>
            <artifactId>legend-pure-next-platform-java-pure</artifactId>
            <version>${project.version}</version>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
            <version>5.10.2</version>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <!-- The extension's grammar, staged under this module's ANTLR package. Lexer and parser must
                 land in ONE directory or `tokenVocab = DiagramLexer` cannot resolve. -->
            <plugin>
                <artifactId>maven-resources-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>3.3.1</version>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>stage-grammar</id>
                        <phase>generate-sources</phase>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>copy-resources</goal>
                        </goals>
                        <configuration>
                            <outputDirectory>${project.build.directory}/antlr4/${antlr.package.dir}</outputDirectory>
                            <resources>
                                <resource>
                                    <directory>${extension.dir}/code/grammar/antlr</directory>
                                    <includes>
                                        <include>*.g4</include>
                                    </includes>
                                </resource>
                            </resources>
                        </configuration>
                    </execution>
                    <!-- Its manifest, read at startup by the engine: the Pure elements that parse a
                         `###Diagram` section and supply its compiler passes, and the grammar's name and
                         entry rule. Staged under the same `languages/` prefix the engine uses for its
                         own, because one reader reads both. -->
                    <execution>
                        <id>stage-language</id>
                        <phase>process-resources</phase>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>copy-resources</goal>
                        </goals>
                        <configuration>
                            <outputDirectory>${project.build.outputDirectory}/languages</outputDirectory>
                            <resources>
                                <resource>
                                    <directory>${extension.dir}</directory>
                                    <includes>
                                        <include>language_diagram.json</include>
                                    </includes>
                                </resource>
                            </resources>
                        </configuration>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.antlr</groupId>
                <artifactId>antlr4-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>4.13.2</version>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>antlr</id>
                        <phase>generate-sources</phase>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>antlr4</goal>
                        </goals>
                        <configuration>
                            <sourceDirectory>${project.build.directory}/antlr4</sourceDirectory>
                            <outputDirectory>${project.build.directory}/generated-sources/antlr4</outputDirectory>
                            <visitor>true</visitor>
                            <listener>false</listener>
                        </configuration>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>
            <!-- The extension's translated Pure — meta::pure::diagram's metamodel, protocol, parser
                 rules and compiler passes — written here by `just java::generate-diagram`, exactly as
                 the engine's own generated/ is written by its generate-* steps. It compiles against the
                 engine's generated metamodel, which is what the dependency direction is for.

                 generated/ sits BESIDE target/, not inside it: `mvn clean` owns target/ and would
                 delete the translator's output, leaving a module that cannot compile. Maven alone
                 cannot build this module from a clean checkout for the same reason the engine cannot —
                 the transform has to RUN first. -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.codehaus.mojo</groupId>
                <artifactId>build-helper-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>1.9.1</version>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>add-translated-sources</id>
                        <phase>generate-sources</phase>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>add-source</goal>
                        </goals>
                        <configuration>
                            <sources>
                                <source>${project.basedir}/generated</source>
                            </sources>
                        </configuration>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
                <configuration>
                    <compilerArgs>
                        <arg>-nowarn</arg>
                    </compilerArgs>
                </configuration>
            </plugin>
            <!-- The tests reach shared/*.pdb and the extension's build/*.pdb at the repository root. -->
            <plugin>
                <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>3.2.5</version>
                <configuration>
                    <workingDirectory>${repo.dir}</workingDirectory>
                </configuration>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>
</project>
